# Windows host, Docker on LXC

This machine is Windows. Do not run `docker`, `docker compose`, or image builds locally.

When containers are needed, SSH to the Muse LXC. Create that LXC only when the user asks. Until a real hostname exists, use the placeholder `muse-lxc`:

```bash
ssh muse-lxc -- docker ps
ssh muse-lxc -- docker compose -f /path/to/compose.yml up -d
```

Local work is `yarn` / `npm` (`lint`, `test`, `typecheck`, `yarn dev`). Docker is for the deployed bot on the LXC, which is how the bot reaches Navidrome on the LAN.

Do not assume Docker Desktop, WSL Docker, or a reachable LXC until the user says it exists.
